# Keep the build context small and free of secrets.
#
# Without this file `docker build` uploads the whole working tree — including
# node_modules, .git, local databases and .env — which is slow and puts real
# credentials into the build context and the layer cache.
#
# The Dockerfile installs dependencies from package.json + pnpm-lock.yaml and
# compiles from src/ only, so none of the following is needed to build.

# Dependencies and build output (rebuilt inside the image)
node_modules
dist

# Admin console UI — not shipped in the image at all. The Dockerfile builds
# the server only (pnpm run build:server), so neither the source nor its
# output is needed in the build context.
admin
admin-dist

# Secrets and local state
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
data
*.sqlite
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# VCS and CI
.git
.gitignore
.github
.changeset

# Tooling, editors, local caches
.vscode
.idea
.claude
.gitnexus
coverage
*.log

# Docs and design assets — not used at build or run time.
# NOTE: config/ is deliberately NOT ignored here even though the Dockerfile
# does not copy it, so that adding a COPY later works without surprise.
docs
*.md
!README.md
